<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="fr-onion" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>French Onion Soup (Famous Barr)</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>3 pounds yellow onions, peeled and thinly sliced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons paprika</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 bay leaf</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{3}{4}</m> cup flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 quarts vegetable broth</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 teaspoons salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup dry wine</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Melt the butter in a Dutch oven.  Add the slices onions and saute slowly over low heat for about <m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> to 2 hours.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the paprika, bay leaf, and flour.  Stir to mix.  Saute over low heat for another 10 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Slowly add the broth (it is easier to avoid lumps if the broth is hot).  Then add the wine.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Simmer uncovered for about 2 hours, stirring occasionally.  Season to taste with salt.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Serve soup in bowls, top with a slice of french bread and top with gruyere (or swiss and mozzarella).  Melt the cheese.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>